{"issues":[{"id":1,"title":"Water Supply Issues in Akonkora Community","community":"Akonkora","status":"pending_assessment","priority":"high","submittedBy":"John Mensah","submittedById":"user_001","submissionDate":"2024-12-01T08:30:00Z","lastUpdated":"2024-12-03T14:20:00Z","category":"Infrastructure","sector":"Water & Sanitation","description":"Community has been without clean water supply for over 2 weeks. The main borehole has broken down and residents are struggling to access clean water. This is affecting over 500 households in the area. Children are missing school to walk long distances to fetch water from neighboring communities.","detailedDescription":"The main borehole serving the Akonkora community was installed in 2018 and has been the primary source of clean water for over 500 households. On November 15, 2024, the submersible pump failed, leaving the entire community without access to clean water. Residents have reported that the pump made unusual noises for several days before completely failing. Local technicians attempted basic repairs but determined that the pump motor has burned out and requires replacement.","location":{"address":"Akonkora, Sefwi Wiawso Constituency","gps":"5.8845° N, 2.4900° W","nearestLandmark":"Akonkora Primary School","accessRoute":"Main road to Sefwi Wiawso, then 3km dirt road east"},"submitter":{"name":"John Mensah","role":"Community Representative","phone":"+233 24 123 4567","email":"john.mensah@community.gh","alternateContact":"Mary Asante (+233 20 987 6543)"},"impactAssessment":{"affectedPopulation":500,"householdsAffected":95,"estimatedCost":25000,"urgencyLevel":"high","environmentalImpact":"medium","economicImpact":"high","socialImpact":"high"},"attachments":[{"id":"att_001","name":"broken_borehole.jpg","type":"image","size":"2.3 MB","url":"/uploads/issues/1/broken_borehole.jpg","uploadDate":"2024-12-01T08:35:00Z"},{"id":"att_002","name":"community_petition.pdf","type":"document","size":"1.1 MB","url":"/uploads/issues/1/c